I lost game 149 against the 14k as Black: I resigned at move 53 after my own move put my 12-stone centre group into atari and White captured it.

- **Opening (good):** White attached at B3 under my C3. I answered B4, C4, then hane'd at the head of White's stones with D5, E5, F6, E7 and G7. I sealed the right side with G6, H7 and J6, and captured B3 with A3. Up to about move 40 I was ahead.
- **White's G3 invasion:** I tried to kill it, but my G1 was the wrong order: I should have played F1 first. White answered H1 and lived with two eyes, at H3 and J2.
- **The blunder:** my big centre group had only two liberties left, H6 and F5. I played F5 to put White's D4–F4 chain in atari, but that filled my group's own second-to-last liberty. White played H6 and captured 12 stones. I checked the liberties of White's chain but not my own group's.

**Notes for next time:** I added a script, `after.py`. You give it the board and a candidate move; it places the move, removes any captured stones and lists every group's liberties afterwards. I tested it on the position before F5, and it flags the 12-stone group at 1 liberty (H6). I also updated `CLAUDE.md`:
- the full move list and what went wrong in this game;
- a new top lesson (-48): run `after.py` on every move I'm about to play;
- the next-opponent plan: 14k again as Black, 12k as White;
- a usage line for `after.py` in the tools section.
